00:37:14,070 --> 00:37:17,880
Christof Koch是世界上最著名的
Christof Koch is one of the foremost neurobiologists

661
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:19,260
神经生物学家之一。
in the world.

662
00:37:19,260 --> 00:37:21,910
他是西雅图保罗艾伦大脑研究所
He is chief scientist at Paul Allen Institute

663
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:24,880
的首席科学家。
for brain research in Seattle.

664
00:37:24,890 --> 00:37:28,890
对于Christof来说，思维纯粹是
For Christof, the mind is purely a product of the web

665
00:37:28,890 --> 00:37:31,780
大脑神经元网络的产物。
of neurons in the brain.

666
00:37:31,780 --> 00:37:34,260
如果互联网是一个大脑，
So if the Internet were a brain,

667
00:37:34,260 --> 00:37:39,370
那么它要有多复杂才能比得上人脑？
how would its complexity stack up against a human brain?

668
00:37:39,370 --> 00:37:40,600
互联网目前
The Internet is, by far,

669
00:37:40,600 --> 00:37:43,490
是最复杂的人造物。
the most complex artifact ever built by mankind.

670
00:37:43,490 --> 00:37:48,110
连接它的晶体管数比典型的
It has on the order of probably 10,000 more transistors

671
00:37:48,110 --> 00:37:50,610
人脑中突触的数量还要多10000个，
than there are synapses in your typical brain.

672
00:37:50,610 --> 00:37:53,050
这当然就引起了一种可能，
It certainly raises the possibility,

673
00:37:53,050 --> 00:37:55,550
因为赋予了互联网极大的复杂性，
given the enormous complexity of the Internet,

674
00:37:55,550 --> 00:37:57,720
现在，也可能是未来某时，
that now, or sometime in the future,

675
00:37:57,720 --> 00:38:00,000
我们会发觉互联网是某种东西，
it may feel like something to be the Internet,

676
00:38:00,010 --> 00:38:03,170
互联网本身产生了某种程度的意识。
that the Internet itself has some degree of sentience.

677
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:08,960
Freeman：有些人认为互联网早已产生了知觉，
Freeman: Some say the Internet may already be sentient

678
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:12,730
或自我意识，但其意识程度
or self-aware, but its level of consciousness may be similar

679
00:38:12,730 --> 00:38:14,600
可能只类似于新生儿。
to that of a newborn.

680
00:38:14,600 --> 00:38:17,970
假如互联网有了某种模糊的意识，
Let's say the Internet has some sort of dim awareness.

681
00:38:17,970 --> 00:38:21,070
我们需要知道这种意识的智慧程度，
We have to ask how intelligent is that awareness.

682
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:22,310
比如你是一个婴儿，
You know, if you're a little baby,

683
00:38:22,310 --> 00:38:24,360
你对自己的母亲具有某种模糊的意识，
you can be somewhat dimly aware of your mom,

684
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:26,410
你会觉得饿，就会找奶喝，
and that you're hungry, and that you're looking for milk,

685
00:38:26,410 --> 00:38:27,860
但你并不会非常智慧，
but you're not really very intelligent

686
00:38:27,870 --> 00:38:29,830
也不会做很多事。
and you're not able to do a lot.

687
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:31,030
Freeman：但很可能
Freeman: But presumably,

688
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:34,000
互联网会学习和进化，
the Internet will learn and evolve.

689
00:38:34,010 --> 00:38:36,290
它会成长。
It will grow up.

690
00:38:36,290 --> 00:38:40,760
如果真是这样，我们又怎么知道
If it does, how will we know when it has become more than

691
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:44,160
它何时不再是名义上的计算机器了？
just a glorified calculator?

692
00:38:44,170 --> 00:38:49,690
一种对意识的测试方法是图灵测试，
One way to gauge consciousness is to apply the turing test.

693
00:38:49,690 --> 00:38:54,840
其方法是对一个人或一部机器问一些问题，
This imagines asking a man and a machine a series of questions

694
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:59,150
询问者却不知道答案是人还是机器给出的，
without knowing who or what is giving the answers.

695
00:38:59,150 --> 00:39:01,950
如果你不能分辨出哪个答案是机器回答的，
If you can't figure out which one is the machine,

696
00:39:01,950 --> 00:39:05,240
机器可以让你认为它是一个人，
if the machine has fooled you into thinking it is human,

697
00:39:05,240 --> 00:39:10,460
那么就能说明这部机器是有智慧的。
then for all practical purposes, it might as well be intelligent.

698
00:39:10,460 --> 00:39:14,530
我应该看哪里？看着你？看着我。
Where do I look? At you? At me.

699
00:39:14,530 --> 00:39:16,410
[相机快门声]
[ Shutter clicks ]

700
00:39:16,410 --> 00:39:19,010
Freeman: Christof提出了一种经过改进的新式图灵测试，
Freeman: Christof proposes a new, improved Turing test

701
00:39:19,020 --> 00:39:22,390
不仅能够用来衡量智力，
that measures not just intelligence,

702
00:39:22,390 --> 00:39:24,420
还能衡量意识。
but consciousness.

703
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:26,540
这种测试使用的是视觉意象。
The test uses visual imagery.

704
00:39:26,540 --> 00:39:30,390
计算机需要判断一系列照片中
The computer must decide whether a series of photographs

705
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:33,350
哪些是真的，哪些是假的。
are right or wrong.

706
00:39:33,350 --> 00:39:35,820
只要是人类一眼就能看出来
Any humans looking at these photographs would know

707
00:39:35,820 --> 00:39:38,050
这些图片都不是真的，
they are not real,

708
00:39:38,050 --> 00:39:42,270
但当代计算机仍能轻易的被欺骗。
but modern day computers are still easily fooled.

709
00:39:42,270 --> 00:39:45,690
除非计算机能得到一个非常非常复杂的列表，
A computer, unless you provide it with a very, very large list,

710
00:39:45,690 --> 00:39:48,160
无限复杂的列表，列出所有可能的情况，
an almost infinite large list of all the exceptions,

711
00:39:48,160 --> 00:39:49,750
这台计算机才能判断图片真假，
could not deal with that.

712
00:39:49,750 --> 00:39:51,530
这也是视觉意识图灵测试的
And that's the basic nature of this turing test

713
00:39:51,530 --> 00:39:53,280
本质特征。
for visual consciousness.

714
00:39:53,290 --> 00:39:55,750
Freeman:Christof打算让互联网
Freeman: Christof wants to apply this test

715
00:39:55,750 --> 00:39:58,040
进行这种测试。
to the entire Internet.

716
00:39:58,040 --> 00:40:01,930
如果庞大的全球计算机网络通过了这项测试，
If the vast global network of computers passes the test,

717
00:40:01,930 --> 00:40:06,100
根据他的标准，就说明互联网是有意识的。
by his definition, it is awake and aware.

718
00:40:06,100 --> 00:40:08,720
那如果互联网已经具有意识了呢？
But what if the Internet is conscious?

719
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:11,720
它会想要什么？它又会如何行动？
What would it want? How will it behave?

720
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:16,970
它会是朋友，还是敌人？仆人，还是主宰？
Will it be friend or foe, servant or master?

721
00:40:16,980 --> 00:40:19,760
如果互联网能够做出独立的行为
To the extent that the Internet developed independent behaviors

722
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:21,730
将会是可怕的，会非常可怕，
would be scary, could be very scary.

723
00:40:21,730 --> 00:40:25,600
虽然它会涉及到所有的安全问题，
Of course, it could have all sorts of security implication.

724
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,570
但在这种程度上来说，我们就能够确定
To that extent, that would certainly be a signal that

725
00:40:27,570 --> 00:40:29,950
互联网中自发产生了某种自主的东西。
there's something independent, autonomous there.

726
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:34,540
Freeman: 如果互联网开始做出一些我们无法预测的事情，
Freeman: If the Internet begins to do unpredictable things,

727
00:40:34,540 --> 00:40:38,290
我们就能知道一种新的生命形式诞生了。
we will know we are dealing with a new form of life.

728
00:40:38,300 --> 00:40:40,710
它也许仍会遵循
It may even follow an important precedent

729
00:40:40,720 --> 00:40:44,250
地球生命重要的历史先例--
in the biological history of planet earth --

730
00:40:44,250 --> 00:40:48,290
同化更小更简单的生物，
the absorption of smaller, simpler life forms

731
00:40:48,290 --> 00:40:52,890
将其组合成更大更复杂的生物。
into the bodies of larger, more complex ones.

732
00:40:52,890 --> 00:40:57,400
人类的未来也许和线粒体很类似，
The future of humanity may be similar to that of mitochondria,

733
00:40:57,400 --> 00:41:01,930
线粒体是大多数细胞的能量工厂。
the power generators inside most biological cells.

734
00:41:01,940 --> 00:41:06,070
线粒体曾经是独立的生物体，
Mitochondria were once independent organisms,

735
00:41:06,070 --> 00:41:07,990
但在进化史上，
but over evolutionary history,

736
00:41:07,990 --> 00:41:11,110
它们被大型细胞所同化，
they were taken over by larger cells.

737
00:41:11,110 --> 00:41:13,580
曾经独立的线粒体
The once-independent mitochondria

738
00:41:13,580 --> 00:41:17,750
变成了它们主人(大型细胞)的能量源。
became a mere power source for their Masters.

739
00:41:17,750 --> 00:41:21,620
我们，以及像超级大国这样的人类文明，
We, and the civilizations we now think of as superpowers,

740
00:41:21,620 --> 00:41:26,180
也许会被我们自己创造的东西所同化。
may be absorbed by our own creation.

741
00:41:26,180 --> 00:41:31,760
但它能从我们身上得到什么呢？除了偶尔修修东西而已？
But what would it want from us,
【原字幕是But what would it wa front,】other than occasional repairs?

742
00:41:31,770 --> 00:41:34,600
或许是需要我们产生的能量，
Perhaps it would want our energy.

743
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:41,060
或许它渴望得到自己并不具有的东西--
Or perhaps it will desire the one thing it doesn't have --

744
00:41:41,060 --> 00:41:43,340
灵魂。
a soul.

745
00:41:43,340 --> 00:41:44,480
灵魂说起来的确挺吓人的，
The soul is really spooky.

746
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:46,700
如果无法衡量它，你又为什么需要它？
If you can't measure it, why do you need it?

747
00:41:46,700 --> 00:41:50,350
如果你没有物理载体，
What function does it do that you can't do

748
00:41:50,350 --> 00:41:52,150
又何必需求它的功能呢？
with physical stuff anymore?

749
00:41:52,150 --> 00:41:54,150
所以今天，随着计算机的发展，
So today, with the existence of computers,

750
00:41:54,160 --> 00:41:55,710
互联网根本不需要灵魂的载体，
there isn't any need for soul stuff,

751
00:41:55,710 --> 00:41:57,910
因为通过软件中的各种算法进行计算
because it can all be done using computations,

752
00:41:57,910 --> 00:41:59,960
它就能得到自己想要的。
using algorithms in software.

753
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:03,210
Freeman: 具有意识和强大力量的互联网，
Freeman: A conscious, superpowerful Internet

754
00:42:03,210 --> 00:42:05,920
也许并不需要灵魂，
may not need a soul to function,

755
00:42:05,920 --> 00:42:09,390
但体会着人类的欢乐和悲伤，
but experiencing the joys and sorrows of humanity

756
00:42:09,390 --> 00:42:13,540
也许会给互联网一种新的方式来理解世界。
would give it another way to understand the world.

757
00:42:13,540 --> 00:42:17,210
不过与人类始终领先的技术间的差距
So our defining difference from technology

758
00:42:17,210 --> 00:42:19,400
会防止人类
may ultimately keep the human race

759
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:22,550
最终变成自己的受害者。
from becoming its victim.

760
00:42:22,550 --> 00:42:25,320
纵观历史，
Throughout history,

761
00:42:25,320 --> 00:42:30,990
每项技术进步都引发了新的战争方式，
every technological advance has led to new forms of warfare.

762
00:42:30,990 --> 00:42:34,860
铜器时代赋予我们斧和剑，
The Bronze Age gave us the ax and the sword.

763
00:42:34,860 --> 00:42:39,280
铁器时代给了我们枪炮，
Iron gave us the cannon and the gun.

764
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:44,120
信息时代催生了属于它自己的武器，
The Information Age has birthed its own weapons.

765
00:42:44,120 --> 00:42:46,170
但信息不像物理资源
But information is not a physical resource

766
00:42:46,170 --> 00:42:48,540
可被开发和控制，
that can be mined and controlled,

767
00:42:48,540 --> 00:42:50,960
像铁和铜一样，
like iron and bronze.

768
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:53,910
它是思维的资源。
It's a resource of the mind.

769
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:57,600
在这样的新时代，一个国家的命运，
In this new age, the fate of a nation,

770
00:42:57,600 --> 00:43:01,880
包括最强大的超级大国，都要依赖于一个东西--
even the mightiest superpower rests on one thing --

771
00:43:03,360 --> 00:43:07,150
那就是人类的想象力。
the power of human imagination.

